# vvaharness/util/config.py

The one fail-safe reader for a dotted configuration key, shared by every stage. Every `knob("dotted.key", default=v)` in this rendering means this function.

Source: `vvaharness/util/config.py` (lines 1-27)
Executor: code
Called from: every stage and backend that reads a setting (for example `vvaharness/pipeline/stages/s4_deepdive.py`, `vvaharness/orchestrator/scan.py`)

// src: vvaharness/util/config.py:19-27
fn knob(cfg, path, default):executor=code {
  node = cfg
  for each part in path split on ".", {
    node = attribute `part` of node, or null when absent
    if (node == null) return default
  }
  return node
  // preserved: "Silent-failure by design": no configuration object, a missing key and an explicit null ALL read as `default`; a setting explicitly set to null in a profile can never mean null at a read site
}
